  "body": "\n_fused_group_barrier (fused_indexer.py) and _group_barrier (persistent_topk.py) let thread zero issue the CTA's release arrival without first synchronizing the CTA. The release orders only writes that thread zero has observed, so histogram bins and state another warp published just before the barrier (for example the red_add_global_i32 coarse bins in the fused cooperative merge, or the atomic_add_global_i32 histogram flush and next-histogram clear in persistent top-k) can still be in flight when other CTAs pass the barrier. Add sync_threads() before the arrival, as b12x did for the fused barrier in 2b6d2005.\n\nThe new test delays one warp per CTA by (cta + 1) * 200K cycles before it publishes a global flag, crosses the barrier, and checks that every CTA sees all four flags. On DGX Spark (GB10, SM121):\n- before: both barriers fail deterministically (missing flags per CTA [3, 2, 1, 0]).\n- with this change: both pass.\n- test_persistent_topk_gpu, test_dsa_indexer_mxfp4, test_glm_pool and test_indexer_kernel_bindings: same results before and after (41 passed; test_chunked_pool_production_compiled_graph[4096-4-*] fails identically without this change, 3 of 540,672 elements off by one).\n\nContext: GLM-5.3 Flash decode routes up to 16 rows through the fused indexer. This race was found while auditing grid barriers after the GLM TP4 device error 6 fixes (#16, #18); it has not been tied to an observed failure. Performance impact not measured; the change adds one CTA barrier per grid barrier.",
